[tools:ca4ed04b-6ec6-f666-7403-2dd6dd2f6acc] [AIMessage] 1. **Evans 1925 – main 
digitized volume entry (with DOI, download links, contents)**  
- **Title:** Evans, Arthur J.: “The ring of Nestor”. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after‑world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet‑rings and bead‑seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia  
- **URL:** https://digi.ub.uni-heidelberg.de/diglit/evans1925?ui_lang=eng  
- **Publisher/Host:** Universitätsbibliothek Heidelberg (Heidelberg University 
Library)  
- **Date:** London 1925 (digitized online since 17.06.2008; last change 
27.07.2023)  
- **Source type:** Digitized monograph (full facsimile, OCR’d PDF available)  
- **Triggered by query:** `"The ring of Nestor" Evans 1925 Heidelberg diglit`  
- **Relevance:** This is the canonical digitized edition of Evans’s 1925 
monograph, providing the full text and plates (Tafeln I–V). The PDF/zoom 
facsimile must be used directly to locate physical measurements, weight, and 
metallurgical remarks.  
- **Key excerpts / notes:**  
  1. “Evans, Arthur J. ‘The ring of Nestor’. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia. London, 1925.”  
  2. “Please cite this volume by using the following URL/DOI: 
**https://doi.org/10.11588/diglit.808** … URN: 
**urn:nbn:de:bsz:16-diglit-8085**.”  
  3. “Content … * [1–42 I. Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia] … * [43–75 II. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after-world] … * [Tafel I – V].”  
  4. Download options: “normal, 49 MB” and “groß, 175 MB” (PDFs), which contain 
all pages and plates where the technical data (dimensions, weight, material 
description) must be read from the original pages/figure captions.  

2. **Evans 1925 – scroll interface / content navigation**  
- **Title:** Evans, Arthur J.: “The ring of Nestor”. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after‑world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet‑rings and bead‑seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia – scroll view for p. 14 (example)  
- **URL:** https://digi.ub.uni-heidelberg.de/diglit/evans1925/0014/scroll  
- **Publisher/Host:** Universitätsbibliothek Heidelberg  
- **Date:** (same digitization context as above; page-level URL)  
- **Source type:** Page‑level facsimile viewer for the monograph  
- **Triggered by query:** `"The ring of Nestor" Evans 1925 Heidelberg diglit`  
- **Relevance:** Confirms structure and provides the page‑scroll UI where 
individual pages (for text) and plates (Tafel I–V) can be accessed. The exact 
measurements/weight will be on specific numbered pages and in plate captions, 
which must be located manually within this viewer or in the downloadable PDF.  
- **Key excerpts / notes:**  
  1. “Content … + Titelblatt + 1–42 I. Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings 
and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia + 43–75 II. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after-world + Tafel I – V.”  
  2. “Seiten verschieben: mit Maus »klicken und ziehen« … (zwei Seiten) 
weiterblättern: Pfeiltasten [←] und [→] oder Seite »anklicken«.”  
  3. The scroll view is the interface you’ll use to reach the relevant 
descriptive text pages and plates (e.g., Tafel I–V), which are expected to 
contain the ring’s measurements and discussions of the gold alloy.  
  4. No measurements are visible in the UI help text itself; they must be taken 
from the facsimile images of the pages once navigated to the correct page/plate 
numbers within this same resource.
