"20260628181455056219_0185510c", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"Evans称其中一枚大型金戒为“涅斯托尔之戒”，其尺寸明显大于普通戒指，属印章戒，戒面
为椭圆形浮雕场景，描绘树木、神祇与超自然存在，被解释为迈锡尼时期关于亡者世界与来
世的视觉表现。", "source_ids": ["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": 
[1]}, {"id": "20260628181455147857_8d945568", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"文中对戒指的重量、形状以及工艺进行技术性描述，指出为高纯度黄金制作，并与克里特
及其他爱琴地区的金印戒进行比较，以确定其年代与文化归属。", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628181455241480_3c2938d2", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"Evans还对戒指的图像进行细致分析，将其与荷马传统、弥诺斯宗教意象和葬礼仪式联系，
强调其在理解迈锡尼宗教与来世观方面的独特重要性。", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628181455340980_7c58a539", "type": "Evidence", "text": "页面标题明确为“The
ring of Nestor. A glimpse into the Minoan after-world and a sepulchral treasure 
of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia”，并标明该数字化文献 
DOI：https://doi.org/10.11588/diglit.808。", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628181455458985_cee54fd2", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"说明中指出内容为一批 Thisbê（玻俄提亚）出土的“sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet-rings and 
bead-seals”，其中包括“涅斯托尔之戒”，该文献由海德堡大学图书馆数字化并公开，使用 
Public Domain Mark 授权。", "source_ids": ["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628181455569715_0e1fc00e", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": 
"影像版包含原文版式、插图和考古图版，可查看戒指的具体图像、尺寸标注及其与墓葬其
他物品的关系。", "source_ids": ["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations": 
[2]}, {"id": "20260628181455671849_e4c392c3", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"作为大学图书馆馆藏的数字版，此页面记录作品标题、作者、出版信息与永久链接（DOI、
URN），可视作一个机构性目录条目。", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628181616516056_c020c24f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The object known as 
the \"Ring of Nestor\" is a large gold signet ring, significantly bigger than an
ordinary finger ring, with an oval bezel bearing a relief scene of trees, 
deities and supernatural beings that has been interpreted as a Mycenaean visual 
representation of the world of the dead and the afterlife.", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628181616712010_8ce66af0", "type": "Claim", "text": "According to Evans’s 
technical description, the \"Ring of Nestor\" is made of high‑purity gold and 
was treated as a signet ring rather than a standard personal ornament.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628181616864683_6a4c8fa1", "type": "Claim", "text": "The \"Ring of 
Nestor\" comes from a sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings and bead‑seals 
excavated from a rock‑cut tomb near the village of Dombrena, close to Thisbê in 
Boeotia, dating to the Late Mycenaean period.", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453747245_86fe6712", "20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations":
[1, 2]}, {"id": "20260628181617060387_d314f7ac", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 
scholarly designation \"Ring of Nestor\" is a name coined by Arthur Evans for 
one particular large gold signet ring from the Thisbê tomb treasure, used as a 
descriptive and interpretive label rather than an ancient title.", "source_ids":
["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628181617236604_a7d0170a", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Heidelberg 
University Library provides an institutional catalog entry and digitized 
facsimile for Arthur Evans’s 1925 publication \"The ring of Nestor. A glimpse 
into the Minoan after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\", accessible via DOI 
https://doi.org/10.11588/diglit.808.", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628182019104653_a142dd25", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
described by Evans as a large gold signet ring made of high‑purity gold, 
significantly larger than ordinary rings, with an oval relief bezel depicting 
trees, deities, and supernatural beings; he interprets the scene as a Mycenaean 
visual representation of the world of the dead and the afterlife.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628181453747245_86fe6712"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628182019354901_c7282d04", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans’s study reports
that the Ring of Nestor forms part of a sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings
and bead seals discovered in a rock‑cut tomb near the village of Dombrena by 
Thisbê in Boeotia, dated to the Late Mycenaean period.", "source_ids": 
["20260628181453747245_86fe6712", "20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations":
[1, 2]}, {"id": "20260628182019555974_b82a160a", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 
Ring of Nestor is cataloged institutionally through the Heidelberg University 
Library’s digital entry for Evans’s 1925 publication \"The ring of Nestor. A 
glimpse into the Minoan after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia,\" which provides a permanent 
DOI link (https://doi.org/10.11588/diglit.808), records bibliographic metadata 
such as title, author, publication information, DOI and URN, and includes 
digitized plates where the ring’s image and dimension markings can be viewed.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628182019922097_567e4f43", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Heidelberg 
University Library’s digital page for Evans’s \"The ring of Nestor\" classifies 
the work as a public domain digital resource (Public Domain Mark), functioning 
as an institutional catalog record for the publication that discusses the Ring 
of Nestor and the sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings and bead seals from 
Thisbê.", "source_ids": ["20260628181453787298_5a75f9f3"], "citations": [2]}], 
"offset": 0, "limit": 20, "total": 17, "next_offset": null}
